intro:
  - >-
    Growing teams need more than individual design files. They need a shared
    system that makes good decisions easier to repeat.
  - >-
    A clear design system connects brand rules, reusable components and content
    patterns across every customer touchpoint.
sections:
  - title: 1. Start With Shared Principles
    description: >-
      Before creating components, define the principles that guide decisions.
      This keeps the system useful when a new page or campaign does not fit an
      existing template.
  - title: 2. Turn Repetition Into Reusable Patterns
    description: >-
      Reusable patterns help teams move faster without creating a collection of
      disconnected one-off solutions.
secondarySections:
  - title: 3. Keep the System Easy to Use
    description: >-
      The best system is documented clearly, easy to find and simple enough for
      the whole team to apply with confidence.
---

A strong design system gives teams the clarity to move quickly without losing
the character that makes a brand recognizable.
